{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs GNU C++14 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following GNU C++14 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nThe leader of some very secretive organization has decided to invite all other members to a meeting. All members of the organization live in the same town which can be represented as $$$n$$$ crossroads connected by $$$m$$$ two-directional streets. The meeting will be held in the leader's house near the crossroad $$$1$$$. There are $$$k$$$ members of the organization invited to the meeting; $$$i$$$-th of them lives near the crossroad $$$a_i$$$. All members of the organization receive the message about the meeting at the same moment and start moving to the location where the meeting is held. In the beginning of each minute each person is located at some crossroad. He or she can either wait a minute at this crossroad, or spend a minute to walk from the current crossroad along some street to another crossroad (obviously, it is possible to start walking along the street only if it begins or ends at the current crossroad). In the beginning of the first minute each person is at the crossroad where he or she lives. As soon as a person reaches the crossroad number $$$1$$$, he or she immediately comes to the leader's house and attends the meeting.Obviously, the leader wants all other members of the organization to come up as early as possible. But, since the organization is very secretive, the leader does not want to attract much attention. Let's denote the discontent of the leader as follows  initially the discontent is $$$0$$$;  whenever a person reaches the crossroad number $$$1$$$, the discontent of the leader increases by $$$c \\cdot x$$$, where $$$c$$$ is some fixed constant, and $$$x$$$ is the number of minutes it took the person to reach the crossroad number $$$1$$$;  whenever $$$x$$$ members of the organization walk along the same street at the same moment in the same direction, $$$dx^2$$$ is added to the discontent, where $$$d$$$ is some fixed constant. This is not cumulative: for example, if two persons are walking along the same street in the same direction at the same moment, then $$$4d$$$ is added to the discontent, not $$$5d$$$. Before sending a message about the meeting, the leader can tell each member of the organization which path they should choose and where they should wait. Help the leader to establish a plan for every member of the organization so they all reach the crossroad $$$1$$$, and the discontent is minimized.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the GNU C++14 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <queue>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <cmath>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst long long MOD = 1000000007LL;\nconst int MAX_N = 300010;\nconst int MAX_K = 400;\n\ntemplate<typename FlowType, typename CostType>\nclass MinCostMaxFlow {\nprivate:\n    static constexpr FlowType EPS = FlowType(1e-9);\n    \n    struct Edge {\n        int src;\n        int dst;\n        FlowType cap;\n        FlowType flow;\n        CostType cost;\n    };\n    \n    vector<vector<int>> graph;\n    vector<Edge> edgeList;\n    vector<CostType> distance;\n    vector<int> bfsQueue;\n    vector<bool> inBfsQueue;\n    vector<int> parentEdge;\n    int nodeCount;\n    int source;\n    int sink;\n    FlowType flowValue;\n    CostType costValue;\n    \npublic:\n    MinCostMaxFlow(int n, int src, int dst) \n        : nodeCount(n), source(src), sink(dst) {\n        assert(0 <= src && src < n && 0 <= dst && dst < n && src != dst);\n        graph.resize(n);\n        distance.resize(n);\n        inBfsQueue.resize(n, false);\n        parentEdge.resize(n);\n        flowValue = 0;\n        costValue = 0;\n    }\n    \n    void reset() {\n        for (auto& e : edgeList) {\n            e.flow = 0;\n        }\n        flowValue = 0;\n    }\n    \n    void connect(int from, int to, FlowType capFwd, FlowType capBwd, CostType costVal) {\n        assert(0 <= from && from < nodeCount && 0 <= to && to < nodeCount);\n        graph[from].push_back((int)edgeList.size());\n        edgeList.push_back({from, to, capFwd, 0, costVal});\n        graph[to].push_back((int)edgeList.size());\n        edgeList.push_back({to, from, capBwd, 0, -costVal});\n    }\n    \n    bool findAugmentingPath() {\n        fill(distance.begin(), distance.end(), numeric_limits<CostType>::max());\n        bfsQueue.clear();\n        bfsQueue.push_back(source);\n        distance[source] = 0;\n        inBfsQueue[source] = true;\n        int head = 0;\n        bool found = false;\n        \n        while (head < (int)bfsQueue.size()) {\n            int u = bfsQueue[head++];\n            if (u == sink) {\n                found = true;\n            }\n            inBfsQueue[u] = false;\n            \n            for (int idx : graph[u]) {\n                const Edge& e = edgeList[idx];\n                if (e.cap - e.flow > EPS && distance[u] + e.cost < distance[e.dst]) {\n                    distance[e.dst] = distance[u] + e.cost;\n                    parentEdge[e.dst] = idx;\n                    if (!inBfsQueue[e.dst]) {\n                        bfsQueue.push_back(e.dst);\n                        inBfsQueue[e.dst] = true;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        if (found) {\n            FlowType augment = numeric_limits<FlowType>::max();\n            int v = sink;\n            while (v != source) {\n                const Edge& e = edgeList[parentEdge[v]];\n                augment = min(augment, e.cap - e.flow);\n                v = e.src;\n            }\n            \n            v = sink;\n            while (v != source) {\n                Edge& e = edgeList[parentEdge[v]];\n                e.flow += augment;\n                Edge& rev = edgeList[parentEdge[v] ^ 1];\n                rev.flow -= augment;\n                v = e.src;\n            }\n            \n            flowValue += augment;\n            costValue += augment * distance[sink];\n        }\n        \n        return found;\n    }\n    \n    pair<FlowType, CostType> solve() {\n        while (findAugmentingPath()) {}\n        return make_pair(flowValue, costValue);\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    int n, m, k, c, d;\n    cin >> n >> m >> k >> c >> d;\n    \n    int t = k * (n - 1);\n    MinCostMaxFlow<int, int> network(t * n + 2, t * n, t * n + 1);\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < t; i++) {\n        network.connect(i * n, t * n + 1, 100, 0, c * i);\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n            if (i + 1 < t) {\n                network.connect(i * n + j, (i + 1) * n + j, 100, 0, 0);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    for (int i = 1; i <= k; i++) {\n        int x;\n        cin >> x;\n        network.connect(t * n, x - 1, 1, 0, 0);\n    }\n    \n    for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++) {\n        int u, v;\n        cin >> u >> v;\n        u--; v--;\n        \n        for (int j = 0; j < t - 1; j++) {\n            int v1 = j * n + u;\n            int v2 = (j + 1) * n + v;\n            \n            for (int q = 0; q < k; q++) {\n                int cost;\n                if (q == 0) cost = d;\n                else if (q == 1) cost = 4 * d;\n                else cost = d * (2 * q + 1);\n                network.connect(v1, v2, 1, 0, cost);\n            }\n            \n            v1 = j * n + v;\n            v2 = (j + 1) * n + u;\n            \n            for (int q = 0; q < k; q++) {\n                int cost;\n                if (q == 0) cost = d;\n                else if (q == 1) cost = 4 * d;\n                else cost = d * (2 * q + 1);\n                network.connect(v1, v2, 1, 0, cost);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    cout << network.solve().second;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <queue>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <cstring>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst long long INF = 1e18;\n\nstruct Edge {\n    int to, rev;\n    long long cap, flow;\n    long long cost;\n    Edge(int t, int r, long long c, long long co) : to(t), rev(r), cap(c), flow(0), cost(co) {}\n};\n\nclass MinCostMaxFlow {\npublic:\n    vector<vector<Edge>> graph;\n    vector<long long> dist;\n    vector<int> parent_node, parent_edge;\n    int n, source, sink;\n    \n    MinCostMaxFlow(int nodes, int src, int dst) : n(nodes), source(src), sink(dst) {\n        graph.resize(n);\n        dist.resize(n);\n        parent_node.resize(n);\n        parent_edge.resize(n);\n    }\n    \n    void add_edge(int from, int to, long long cap, long long cost) {\n        graph[from].emplace_back(to, graph[to].size(), cap, cost);\n        graph[to].emplace_back(from, graph[from].size() - 1, 0, -cost);\n    }\n    \n    pair<long long, long long> solve() {\n        long long total_flow = 0, total_cost = 0;\n        \n        while (true) {\n            fill(dist.begin(), dist.end(), INF);\n            dist[